# Build-generated files — never line-merge them. They are machine-produced and
# only valid as a complete set from one build run, so a blended hand-merge is
# always wrong. The `generated-newer-wins` driver (registered globally by
# .claude/skills/install.sh, sourced from
# .claude/skills/_lib/merge_drivers/tom_generated_newer_wins.py) keeps the side
# whose build is newer (higher buildNumber / later timestamp) and otherwise
# takes the remote side, so these resolve deterministically on every reconcile
# instead of recurring as conflicts. See the meta CLAUDE.md "Generated-file
# merge conflicts (reconcile policy)" and reconciliation_problem_analysis.md
# § 4.D. If the driver is not registered on a machine, git simply falls back to
# its default merge for these paths (a re-run of install.sh restores it).
**/tom_build_state.json    merge=generated-newer-wins
**/*.versioner.dart        merge=generated-newer-wins
**/*.reflection.dart       merge=generated-newer-wins
